    "lawCode": "Amd §§8-1.0. 8-2.0, 9-8.0, 11-4.0 & 11-12.0, Chap 812 of 1942",
    "lawSection": "Erie County Tax Act",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8324\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the Erie county tax act, in relation to providing that the\namount required to redeem real property affected by any tax sale\ncertificate in foreclosure, or to be recovered by the plaintiff in\nforeclosure, shall include the aggregate amount of all tax sale\ncertificates affecting such real property and shall also include\namounts for attorneys' fees, abstracts of title, court costs, allowances\nand other disbursements\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo provide that the amount required to redeem real property affected\nby any tax sale certificate in foreclosure shall include the\naggregate amount of all tax sale certificates affecting such real\nproperty.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would amend Sections 8-1.0, 8-2.0, 98.0, 11-4.0 and 11-12.0\nof the Erie County Tax Act so that the amount required to redeem real\nproperty affected by any Erie County tax sale certificate in\nforeclosure, or to be recovered by the plaintiff in such foreclosure,\nshall include the aggregate amount of all tax sale certificates\naffecting such real property, together with amounts for reasonable\nand necessary attorney's fees, abstracts of title, court costs,\nallowances and other disbursements.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nBy requiring that the amount required to be paid to redeem such\nproperty, and the amount to be recovered in foreclosure by the owner\nof any Erie County tax sale certificate, shall include the full\namount of all tax sale certificates so-owned, together with accrued\ninterest, penalties and the costs and expenses of foreclosure such as\nreasonable and necessary attorneys' fees, court costs and abstracts\nof title, the value and enforceability of Erie County tax sale\ncertificates offered for sale will be significantly enhanced.\n\nSimilarly, insofar as Erie County may find itself continuing to own\ntax sale certificates, and needing to directly enforce the collection\nof tax delinquencies under the in rem tax foreclosure provisions of\nthe Erie County Tax Act, the legislation provides for the payment or\nrecovery of a \"in rem fee\" of not more than $500 so as to cover the\ncosts to Erie County for such in rem tax foreclosures.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2008: S.6677-B/A.8345-C, Passed the Senate.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided that sections two,\nthree, four and five of this act shall not affect or apply to any\nErie county tax sale certificates for any fiscal year prior to 2010.\n\n",
